WEBVTT

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:09.440
Do you play much sport?

00:00:09.560 --> 00:00:10.640
Not really.

00:00:10.760 --> 00:00:12.160
I occasionally watch the rugby on TV ...

00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:13.400
...but I'm not a big sports fan.

00:00:13.520 --> 00:00:14.720
Did you see the match at the weekend?

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:17.280
Oh, not sport again!

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:21.080
So, have you got any exciting plans for next week?

00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:22.120
Well, er...

00:00:22.240 --> 00:00:23.640
No, not really.

00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:24.920
Just work.

00:00:25.040 --> 00:00:27.120
I've got a lot to do in the shop this week...

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:29.240
...because we're going to a wedding next weekend.

00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:31.880
Oh, the shop? What do you do?

00:00:32.040 --> 00:00:33.520
I'm a florist.

00:00:33.640 --> 00:00:36.080
What a great job! Where's the shop?

00:00:36.240 --> 00:00:38.880
Not far from here. I'll show you some time.

00:00:39.040 --> 00:00:40.120
That would be great!

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:42.400
And are you the manager, or...

00:00:42.720 --> 00:00:45.600
Well, not really...

00:00:45.720 --> 00:00:47.440
...it's my shop.

00:00:47.560 --> 00:00:50.560
Wow. That's amazing!

00:00:50.680 --> 00:00:53.520
So you're a businesswoman!

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:55.240
Do you work on your own?

00:00:55.400 --> 00:00:57.560
No, I have someone to help.

00:00:57.680 --> 00:01:00.160
Tina. She comes in for a few hours every day.

00:01:00.320 --> 00:01:01.480
Oh, that's good.

00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:03.920
How about you? What do you do?

00:01:04.040 --> 00:01:07.720
Oh, marketing. Boring!

00:01:09.080 --> 00:01:11.160
Same as Mark...

00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:13.440
He works in marketing.

00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:16.720
Oh, I'm sorry.

00:01:16.840 --> 00:01:19.320
I find it boring.

00:01:20.600 --> 00:01:22.800
Do you have any plans for the weekend?

00:01:22.960 --> 00:01:25.960
Actually, yes. I'm going to visit my brother, Dan.

00:01:26.200 --> 00:01:28.080
Oh, I remember Dan. How is he?

00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:30.040
He's fine. He's married now.

00:01:30.200 --> 00:01:32.000
To Martina.

00:01:33.640 --> 00:01:35.600
Anyway, we really must go.

00:01:35.720 --> 00:01:37.280
I need to get back to the shop.

00:01:37.400 --> 00:01:38.440
Yeah, of course.

00:01:38.560 --> 00:01:39.600
It was really nice to meet you.

00:01:39.720 --> 00:01:40.720
Yeah, you too.

00:01:40.840 --> 00:01:42.200
Nice to meet you, Mark.

00:01:42.320 --> 00:01:43.880
It was great to see you again, Annie.

00:01:44.040 --> 00:01:45.560
Yeah! We must meet up soon!

00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:46.840
Definitely!

00:01:46.960 --> 00:01:47.920
Actually...

00:01:48.040 --> 00:01:50.920
...it's Leo's birthday in a couple of weeks.

00:01:51.040 --> 00:01:52.840
Perhaps we could meet then.

00:01:52.960 --> 00:01:54.680
OK, great. I'll give you a call.

00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:57.080
And say hello to Dan for me!
